.TH PORTLY 1 "" "" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
portly \- see what uses your ports, and stop it safely
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B portly
.RB [ \-\-all ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-verbose ]
.br
.B portly
.IR port " ..."
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-verbose ]
.br
.B portly stop
.IR port " ..."
.RB [ \-\-yes ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.RB [ \-\-expect
.IR plan-id ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-verbose ]
.br
.B portly completion
.IR shell
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists local TCP and UDP ports, the process or container behind each, and the project it belongs to.
.B stop
shows exactly what would stop, asks, stops it gracefully and checks that the port is free.
A bare port means TCP. Use
.IB port /udp
to stop a UDP owner.
Stopping is enabled only on platforms whose tests have passed. Elsewhere it is refused.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-all
Also list likely-client UDP ports.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print one JSON document. Never prompts. With
.B stop
and without
.B \-\-yes
it stops nothing and returns a plan id.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Do not ask. Every check still runs.
.TP
.B \-\-force
If a graceful stop was delivered and failed, ask for the word kill, then kill. Unsaved data can be lost.
.TP
.BI \-\-expect " plan-id"
Stop only if the targets are the ones inspected earlier.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Print diagnostics on standard error.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help ", " \-v ", " \-\-version
Print help or the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including a lookup of a free port.
.TP
.B 1
Internal error.
.TP
.B 2
Bad usage.
.TP
.B 3
Nothing to stop is listening.
.TP
.B 4
Permission denied or owner unresolved.
.TP
.B 5
Refused.
.TP
.B 6
Confirmation required or cancelled.
.TP
.B 7
A stop was delivered, but the port was not confirmed free.
.TP
.B 8
Several ports with different outcomes.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disables colour.
.TP
.B TERM
The value dumb disables colour.
.TP
.BR DOCKER_HOST ", " DOCKER_CONTEXT
Used to find a local container engine. Remote engines are ignored.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
portly
portly 8000
portly stop 3000 8000
portly stop 8000 \-\-json
.fi
